course: dictionary
lesson: 6
title: A word for a special church
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An abbey is a building, or group of buildings, where monks or nuns live and pray together. Their leader is an abbot for monks or an abbess for nuns. Look at the clues in «Charles was crowned with Queen Camilla at Westminster Abbey». A crowning is a very important event, so the abbey must be a large, special place.
explain: Sometimes abbey means only the big church that was once part of such a place. Westminster Abbey in London is a famous example. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A church, or a building where people gather for a special event. Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Abbey can also be part of a name. «Downton Abbey» is a TV series, so the word there is part of a title. When you see a capital letter, you may be reading a name, not just a common word.
fact: An abbey is a building, or group of buildings, where monks or nuns live and pray together.
fact: An abbot leads an abbey of monks, and an abbess leads an abbey of nuns.
fact: «Westminster Abbey» is a large church in London.
fact: In the news, royal events such as coronations take place at Westminster Abbey.
fact: «Downton Abbey» is the name of a TV series, so the word is part of a title.
exercise: What is an abbey? | *A building where monks or nuns live and pray together | A shop that sells old books | A tall tower on a castle | A kind of bread
exercise: «The old abbey was a ruined building with no roof.» What does ruined mean? | *Badly damaged and falling apart | Brand new and freshly painted | Full of happy people | Covered in gold
exercise: Who leads an abbey of nuns? | A mayor | *An abbess | A chef
test:
In «Charles was crowned with Queen Camilla at Westminster Abbey», where did the crowning happen? | In a shop | *At a large church in London | In a school | On a boat
test:
What is the job of an abbot? | *To lead an abbey of monks | To bake bread for the town | To drive the buses | To teach maths to children
exam: Which word means a building where monks or nuns live and pray together? | Museum | Castle | *Abbey | Palace
